// Relay.xcconfig — where this build's documents come from, out of the box.
//
// The app is meant to work the moment it is installed: no folder to pick, no
// address to type, no token to paste. These two values are what make that true,
// and they are baked into the build rather than asked for at first run.
//
// PENCILLOOP_RELAY_URL has no scheme on purpose. An xcconfig treats `//` as the
// start of a comment, so `https://host` would silently become `https:` — a
// value that looks right in the file and is wrong in the build. The app puts
// the scheme back; it refuses anything that is not https anyway.
//
// The token is a credential. It lives in Config/Local.xcconfig, which is not
// committed, and this file is included from there rather than the other way
// round so a checkout with no local config still builds — it just starts with
// the folder picker, exactly as it did before.

PENCILLOOP_RELAY_URL =
PENCILLOOP_RELAY_TOKEN =
